cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "satellite-landuse-toolkit: land-use, forest-loss and surface-water analysis from free satellite data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and, separately, every upstream dataset you used."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Suzuki
    given-names: Kengo
    affiliation: "Space Seed Holdings Inc."
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # fill in before release
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/satellite-landuse-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A small Python toolkit for land-use analysis of any area on Earth using only
  free, account-free satellite products (ESA WorldCover, Hansen Global Forest
  Change, JRC Global Surface Water, Sentinel-2 L2A, Esri Annual Land Cover).
  It runs locally without Earth Engine or API keys, integrates areas with the
  exact spherical latitude-band formula, and encodes the interpretation rules
  that keep such analyses defensible: tree-cover loss is never reported as
  "remaining forest", two-date comparisons use a common valid-pixel mask, and
  threshold sensitivity is reported alongside every result.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - land cover
  - land use change
  - deforestation
  - surface water
  - Sentinel-2
  - open data
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
